course: dictionary
lesson: 12538
title: Detectable: able to be found
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Detectable means able to be noticed or found. Something detectable can be picked up by your senses, or by a test or a machine such as a thermometer. The word comes from the verb detect, which means to find something.
explain: Read this: «The change in temperature was detectable on the thermometer.» The thermometer is the tool that finds the change, so detectable means the change could be found with a tool. Ask yourself: could someone find it? If yes, the word is detectable.
explain: «The medicine was detectable in his blood test.» The test could find the medicine in his blood. The opposite is undetectable, which means too small or too well hidden for any test to find.
fact: Detectable means able to be noticed or found, especially with tests or instruments.
fact: The opposite of detectable is undetectable.
fact: «Detectable» often goes with a tool, like a thermometer, a microscope or a blood test.
fact: «A barely detectable difference» means a difference so small that you only just notice it.
fact: Detect means to find or notice something, so detectable means it can be found.
exercise: «The change in temperature was detectable on the thermometer.» What does detectable mean here? | Put away safely | *Able to be noticed or measured | Very hot and dangerous | Painted in bright colours
exercise: What is the opposite of detectable? | Happy | *Undetectable | Tiny | Electric
exercise: «The change was barely detectable, so the scientists used a very sensitive machine.» Why did they need a sensitive machine? | Because the change was very big and loud | *Because the change was very small and hard to find | Because the scientists were bored | Because the machine was painted red
test: «Nurses checked the sample, and the drug was detectable in it.» What does detectable mean? | Hard to lift | Very cold | Bright and shiny | *Able to be found by a test
test: Which word means the same as detectable here? «The sugar level was detectable on the meter.» | *Measurable | Silent | Flat | Lost
exam: In «a barely detectable difference», what does barely detectable mean? | *Only just able to be found, very small | Completely invisible for ever | Very loud and easy to hear | Painted on the wall
